// TC-PST-26: foo's non-heap precondition `n > 0` is compatible with its postcondition
// `isPos(n)` (body: n > 0). isPos has no precondition — its axiom fires unconditionally.
// Supervisor's fix adds `n > 0` from foo's own precondition, then checks
// `inhale n > 0; inhale n > 0; assert false` — n > 0 is satisfiable → assert false fails
// → postUnsatisfiable does NOT fire (correct).
// Normal verification also passes: precondition n > 0 directly establishes isPos(n).

pure boolean isPos(int n) = n > 0;

requires n > 0;
ensures isPos(n);
void foo(int n) { }
